    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0218" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./74: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-06-21T16:00:00-04:00">June 21, 1934—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>129. In conversation yesterday about other matters, Troyanovsky said he had been
                    asked by Litvinoff to inquire whether it would be agreeable to us to transfer
                    the debt negotiation to Washington and, upon receiving an affirmative reply, he
                    said he would wire Litvinoff. He seems very willing to take up the matter
                    here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
